WEBVTT

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:13.180
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:13.180
TAKARA FANSUBS

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.830
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.580
Overlooking the rows of houses and stores

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.280
from the highest vantage,

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:26.780
Such things as tears and sadness

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.680
will quickly vanish

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:36.880
The birds, wind, and sunshine...

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.880
...all are your friends

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:45.790
I'll carry this dream farther than far

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:50.390
...no matter the distance...

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:57.590
I long to fly freely

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:01.790
through the blue sky in my heart...

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:04.690
The far distant blue sky

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:12.190
It flows into tomorrow

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:33.230
The God of Death came to Romeo's
house, seeking to buy him.

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:37.730
But Roberto refused, insisting he would
never sell Romeo

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.430
regardless of how hard
the times were.

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:45.080
But that night, Romeo's father
collapsed because of the injury

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:48.080
which he had received in the fire.

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:55.030
Episode 3:

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:55.030
Farewell, My Village

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:05.030
Dear!

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:06.630
Roberto! Hold on!

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:08.730
Roberto! It's me, do you understand?

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:19.830
Romeo...

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:22.250
Won't sell...

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:24.380
Dear!

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:30.430
Romeo...

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:32.830
Won't sell...

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:39.530
Big brother, what's going to happen to Dad?

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:40.830
Is he gonna die?

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:42.330
Of course not!

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:45.330
Dad's strong...

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.930
...the strongest in the whole village.

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:53.230
The disease is attacking his eyes.

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:54.630
His eyes?!

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:58.030
His condition is dangerous.

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:03.020
What on earth can we do to help him?

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:06.130
Calling a doctor is the only way.

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:08.130
In the town of Locaron,

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:10.130
There's a doctor named Baregi.

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:11.630
Considering his notoriety...

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:15.030
I think it's likely he could save Roberto.

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:15.830
How much?

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:18.530
How much would it cost for
this doctor to come?

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:22.830
Father?

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:26.930
Twenty francs.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:28.730
Possibly more.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:39.930
We won't be able to get that kind of money from anywhere!

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:56.230
Twenty francs...

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:10.530
You need this carried, right?

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:13.830
Hey! Take it easy, Romeo!

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:15.330
I want to work!

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.330
I'm sorry...

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:22.830
We heard about Roberto's condition...

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:24.830
Plesase hire me...

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:27.530
I need 20 francs to get a doctor!

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:30.030
I'll clean... chop wood... anything you need!

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:34.230
Tony!

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:36.330
I'm sorry, Romeo...

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:39.430
We have nothing to spare, because of
the drought and fire.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:43.330
We can't even sell these potatoes...

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:45.130
they're our seed-potatoes for next year.

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:52.630
Please God...

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:56.430
Please God, please, I beg you...

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.930
I pray that Dad will get better...

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:00.130
That he will get better...

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:04.330
Carlo! Pedro!

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:05.430
Brother!

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:21.430
Carlo! Let's tell him!

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:23.730
Brother, don't tell anyone!

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:24.830
About what?

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:26.530
Okay now, it's really great.

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:28.530
A secret, ok?

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:32.330
We're gonna call the doctor!

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:34.630
We've got a bunch of money!

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:36.130
We found it!

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:37.530
You mean it?

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:41.330
See!

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:45.730
Isn't it great!

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:47.230
We were hiding it.

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:49.030
How much money is this?

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:50.130
Thats one rappen.

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:52.030
So will the doctor come?

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:55.030
It's not nearly enough.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:00.530
But, if we got a bunch more,
the doctor would come, wouldn't he?

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:02.630
Wouldn't he come then?

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:04.830
Lets go look for more!

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:06.130
Yeah!

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:09.430
Hey! Let's look where we looked before!

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:10.930
Yeah!

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:29.630
Dad... what should I do?

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:54.230
If your father had just agreed to
sell you in the first place,

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:57.190
you wouldn't have had to go through
what happened to your family.

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:05.280
I stretch out my hand as your saviour...

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:07.280
Tell them this:

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:10.330
Be at Scara's shop by the midday bell

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:12.530
and I'll have 25 francs ready.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.530
Twenty five francs?!

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:16.730
I intend to buy you.

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:22.030
See, it was thirty francs last night

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:24.030
but your breadwinner has collapsed now.

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:27.930
So even at five francs less, he will prefer it
to the hand of Death at his throat.

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:29.830
So tell them, and don't forget.

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:32.430
Any later than midday and
it goes down even more.

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:55.430
So tell them, and don't forget.
Be at Scara's shop by midday.

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:56.730
Damn it!

00:07:58.130 --> 00:08:00.230
I beg of you!

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:02.630
We will without fail work and
return the money!

00:08:02.630 --> 00:08:04.230
I hear you, but...

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:08.630
I know I'm asking the impossible, but...

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:10.330
I'm so sorry...

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:12.530
I really want to help, but
I'm also having

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:15.530
such a hard time this year, that...

00:08:16.630 --> 00:08:19.030
I'm truly sorry, Jessica.

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:38.030
The fire has ruined business.

00:08:38.230 --> 00:08:41.130
No customers have come
by except for you.

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:43.230
They'll come.

00:08:44.530 --> 00:08:46.730
Lured here, with twenty five francs as bait.

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:58.580
Hey Romeo! You need anything?

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:03.730
There's something I want to know.

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:08.530
If you bought me, where
would I be taken?

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:09.430
Milan.

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:10.430
Milan?

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:12.430
That's the big city!

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:15.130
It's like a dream there.

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:19.830
You'll work there as a chimney sweep.

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:32.480
I'll go.

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:37.430
l'd like you to call a doctor
with the money.

00:09:38.530 --> 00:09:41.130
So you've decided have you, Romeo?

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:45.030
Bah! Chimney sweeping isn't such
hard work.

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:48.030
It gets a teensy bit tough sometimes,
but just in winter.

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:50.030
And in the spring you can come back.

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:53.130
- Eh? To this town?
- Sure

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:54.430
Kid...

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:58.480
Sign here.

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:03.730
This contract says that
I own you until spring.

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:11.030
Here! Use this.

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:12.930
I... I...

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:14.930
Just an X is fine.

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:20.030
If I sign, you'll call the doctor, right?

00:10:20.130 --> 00:10:21.330
That's right.

00:10:28.130 --> 00:10:29.130
How much is this?

00:10:29.130 --> 00:10:30.430
That's one rappen.

00:10:30.530 --> 00:10:32.530
Will the doctor come?

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:35.330
I know what I'm asking is impossible.

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:38.130
We couldn't get that kind of
money from anywhere.

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:57.330
With this, you are now mine!

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:15.980
It's me, Scara!

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:24.080
Hey there, Jessica...

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:25.580
I brought him here without
a moment's delay.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:28.080
Good evening, madam.

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:29.280
Good sir, you are...?

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:31.380
My name is Baregi.

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:33.080
Brought him straight from Locarno.

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:35.580
Even there, he's a famous doctor.

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:37.580
A doctor?!

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:38.780
But we have no...

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:41.480
Don't worry, it's taken care of.

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:43.780
Just ask Romeo!

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:48.380
Romeo, What does he mean?

00:11:48.380 --> 00:11:49.580
Well...

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:57.180
Romeo... you didn't go to that man...

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:00.180
I... made a promise.

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:02.280
This discussion can wait.

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:03.780
Where's the patient?

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:08.330
Roberto... can you hear me?

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:11.580
- Who is it?
- Darling, it's a doctor.

00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:14.380
Darling!

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:17.180
Quiet! Please don't move.

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:22.380
What's the meaning of this, Jessica?

00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:49.980
Mom...

00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:52.180
How's Dad?

00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:53.380
Sleeping.

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:54.030
So...

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:56.330
Yes, he'll be fine now.

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:59.980
He'll need the bandage for some time,

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:01.680
but he'll be able to see again, for sure.

00:13:01.730 --> 00:13:05.180
Thank goodness. Thank goodness, Mother!

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:13.580
Romeo... what have you done?

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:16.480
Don't worry, Mom.

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:17.680
It's only for half a year.

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:20.380
After half a year, they'll
let me come back...

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:21.780
...that was the promise.

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:25.480
Why didn't you say something
to your mother?

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:30.480
Fretting about so...
Deciding such things... all by yourself.

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:33.680
I'm sorry, Mother.

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:35.280
But... I'll be fine.

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:36.830
After all, it's for Dad's sake.

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:40.380
Romeo!

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:45.980
Forgive your poor helpless mother
as well, unable to do anything.

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:47.130
Forgive me!

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:59.080
Thus the night passed, and
the father was saved.

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:03.080
And then the day after tomorrow came.

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:06.730
The day for Romeo to leave the village.

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:37.980
Tino! Mario! Breakfast!

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:38.780
Yes!

00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:40.180
Where is Anita?

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:42.280
Outside.

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:45.280
Sulking because Romeo leaves today.

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:47.280
It's really something, don't you think?

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:50.730
I hear there's a church as big
as a mountain there.

00:14:50.980 --> 00:14:54.380
There's even supposed to be hundreds or
thousands of shops to see!

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:56.380
It's a dream city!

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:58.680
And you can return in springtime.

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:00.580
Romeo is so lucky!

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:03.280
Gee... I want to go clean chimneys too!

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:05.980
Don't say that! Don't ever say that!

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:06.980
Why?

00:15:07.030 --> 00:15:10.380
"Coming back" is just a futile hope.

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:12.480
That's what Scara said.

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:15.230
Lots of children go to Milan...

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:17.680
But none have returned.

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:19.080
None!

00:15:20.380 --> 00:15:23.480
You mustn't tell this to Romeo's family, understand?

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:25.280
It would be too cruel.

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:29.380
Today turned out to be the last day of work!

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:33.880
Ready? Let's go home, Piccolo.

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:36.480
Romeo!

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:37.880
Don't go!

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:41.180
If you go to Milan, you'll die!

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:44.280
I heard that Scara said

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:46.080
that coming back in the spring is a lie!

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:49.580
The truth is that children who go
to Milan don't come back alive!

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:53.480
But why?

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:55.080
No one knows,

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:57.180
but not even one has returned!

00:15:58.580 --> 00:15:59.880
It can't be...

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:02.480
I beg you!

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:03.680
Please don't go!

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:06.280
I've already promised...

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:08.580
and paid the doctor.

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:11.180
If I don't go, I'll be a coward.

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:15.180
You made a promise to me too!

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:16.180
That when...

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:18.680
when winter came, if it snowed...

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:23.480
I hate you, Romeo!

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:30.880
I'm sorry, Anita...

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:33.280
Romeo!

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:34.580
Please Anita...

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:38.280
Don't say anything about this to Mom or Dad.

00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:41.180
Ok?

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:47.980
Romeo, you fool!

00:16:57.380 --> 00:16:58.780
Rain!

00:17:00.780 --> 00:17:03.780
It's rain! The first rain in five months!

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:12.880
Darling, can you hear it?

00:17:13.080 --> 00:17:15.080
Yes, thank goodness.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:16.980
The village will make it now.

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:19.080
It's like a twist of fortune...

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:20.580
Just as Romeo is leaving...

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:21.680
Yes.

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:25.280
I always thought I was being too sweet to him...

00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:28.680
For him to go like this, for out sakes...

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:33.680
I mustn't cry.

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:39.880
When spring arrives, he will return back to us.

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:43.180
Is that so.. in the spring?

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:44.780
Yes. In the spring.

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:49.780
Jessica...

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:51.080
Roberto!

00:17:51.280 --> 00:17:53.980
Our boy! Our poor boy!

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:29.780
Jessica!

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:34.880
There's something I wanted to
tell Romeo someday.

00:18:37.580 --> 00:18:40.280
The boy thinks I'm a hero...

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:42.680
but he's wrong.

00:18:43.980 --> 00:18:46.280
"You must grow up much bigger..."

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:49.080
"and much more powerful than
even me."

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:51.580
Jessica...

00:18:52.780 --> 00:18:56.180
I'm a man with no education.

00:18:56.980 --> 00:19:00.380
Whats more, I must part from a family
member that I'd give my life for

00:19:00.480 --> 00:19:04.580
because we live in such... poverty.

00:19:10.780 --> 00:19:12.680
But Romeo is different.

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:16.080
He wants to carve out a life
using his own strength

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:17.680
and he really does have
the strength to do it.

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:21.980
This hope...

00:19:22.780 --> 00:19:25.880
is one of my heart's many
wishes for Romeo

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:27.980
but not even one such wish
have I been able to grant him.

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:32.580
Dad...

00:19:34.180 --> 00:19:36.340
Romeo! Is that Romeo?

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:39.180
Dad!

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:42.670
You're wrong! You're a hero!

00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:45.980
I'm going to become strong
like you, Dad.

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:49.880
I won't give up!

00:19:50.780 --> 00:19:53.880
I... I'm...
I'm your kid!

00:19:58.380 --> 00:19:59.480
Romeo...

00:20:03.480 --> 00:20:05.080
Remember, Romeo...

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:06.880
no matter what, have courage.

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:11.180
If something brings tears to your eyes,
then remember us.

00:20:11.280 --> 00:20:12.880
We believe in you.

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:17.580
You are my precious son.

00:20:17.580 --> 00:20:18.880
Dad!

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:22.380
Romeo, I'm proud of you.

00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:34.780
Here's your lunch.

00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:38.480
It's your favourite, cheese and bread.

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:39.780
Thanks!

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:41.480
Big brother!

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:44.180
You won't forget about me?
And me?

00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:45.780
I won't forget.

00:20:45.980 --> 00:20:48.180
Take good care of Piccolo?

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:49.380
Ok.

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:51.280
Mom...

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:03.680
Well!

00:21:03.880 --> 00:21:04.980
I'm going!

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:07.480
Brother!

00:21:11.880 --> 00:21:13.280
Romeo!

00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:16.480
Brother!

00:21:17.780 --> 00:21:19.780
Come back home, Romeo.

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:23.930
I'll come back. Absolutely.

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:30.980
After all, this is... my home!

00:21:32.980 --> 00:21:34.280
The carriage turned toward Milan,

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:36.680
...and sped away.

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:40.080
Romeo had no way of knowing

00:21:40.180 --> 00:21:42.180
of the dreams and friendships,

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:44.680
and the violent tempest of events

00:21:44.880 --> 00:21:47.330
that lay in store for him in Milan.

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:56.460
In met a boy in the rain.

00:21:56.880 --> 00:21:59.480
He says he's also going to become
a chimney sweep...

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:02.380
but he won't tell me
anything but his name.

00:22:03.480 --> 00:22:05.580
All right. I won't ask you any
more questions,

00:22:05.580 --> 00:22:06.580
Alfredo.

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:10.480
Next time:
The Boy on the Poster
See you then!

00:22:12.330 --> 00:22:16.280
"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"

00:22:25.270 --> 00:22:29.370
Si Si Ciao, why do the good times

00:22:29.470 --> 00:22:33.670
seem to end so soon?

00:22:33.870 --> 00:22:37.870
Si Si Ciao, we're all friends

00:22:38.070 --> 00:22:42.070
Let's meet again on these Roman roofs

00:22:42.680 --> 00:22:46.980
Your laughing voice dances

00:22:46.980 --> 00:22:50.880
Once again in the sky

00:22:51.280 --> 00:22:58.180
Your pocket bursting with memories

00:22:59.880 --> 00:23:03.780
Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now

00:23:03.980 --> 00:23:07.980
Let's meet again on these Roman roofs
